 "statement": "Annotated from the Beinecke scan alone (the '70v (part)' canvas that shows two fish, and four quadrant crops of it). A wheel: two fish at the centre with a word in another script between them and two stars; a band of small strokes; an inner ring of ten nude female figures in green-tinted tubs lying along the ring; an outer ring of nineteen nude female figures in upright patterned tubs, six of them with a blue cap or headband, all on the right-hand side. Every figure holds a star on a line and has a short label beside it. The label groups in the transcription have 19, 10 and 1 lines, which matches the outer ring, the inner ring and the labelled star at the centre. Within each ring I paired labels to figures clockwise starting from the figure nearest twelve o'clock; that starting point and direction are an assumption made from the line ids alone, not checked against the words, so the within-ring pairing may be rotated.",
